  <h1>Dengue NS1 vs IgM/IgG Rapid Tests</h1>

  <p><strong>Direct answer:</strong> NS1 antigen detects the dengue virus itself and is most useful in the first week of fever; IgM/IgG antibodies detect the immune response and become more reliable from about day 5 onward. A combined NS1 + IgM/IgG device covers the widest diagnostic window in a single test.</p>

  <h2>Comparison table</h2>
  <div class="card">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th></th><th>NS1 Antigen</th><th>IgM/IgG Antibody</th></tr></thead>
